## Layer 1: Schema Inversion (Adjacency List)

### Scope Contract
Refactor `catalogueItemType.ts` from a top-down `children` array model to a bottom-up `parent` reference model. This flattens the dependency graph in the Content Lake, guaranteeing infinite scaling, trivial GROQ sub-tree queries, and pure CRUD.

### DoD

- [ ] 1.1 — In `sanity/schemaTypes/catalogueItemType.ts`: Remove the `children` array field entirely.
  - Difficulty: 1 - C(sanity/schemaTypes/catalogueItemType.ts): remove children array

- [ ] 1.2 — In `sanity/schemaTypes/catalogueItemType.ts`: Add a `parent` field of type `reference` pointing to `[{ type: "catalogueItem" }]`. Configure it as optional (roots will have no parent). Add a description explaining it forms the recursive tree graph.
  - Difficulty: 1 - A(sanity/schemaTypes/catalogueItemType.ts): add parent reference field

### Verification — Layer 1

- [ ] V1.1 — Run `npx sanity schema extract` (or equivalent) and confirm the `catalogueItem` schema contains `parent` and NO `children` property.
  - Difficulty: 1

