## Layer 2: Seed & Migration Updates

### Scope Contract
Update the logic that writes catalogue items to Sanity to populate the `parent` reference instead of `children` arrays.

### DoD

- [ ] 2.1 — In `scripts/migrate-catalogue-to-flat.mjs` (if it exists) or `scripts/seed-catalogue.mjs`: Modify the tree flattening logic. When recursively walking the `RAW_CATALOGUE`, pass the current node's `_id` down to its children as their `parentId`. When creating the child document object, add `parent: { _type: 'reference', _ref: parentId }` instead of building a `children` array on the parent.
  - Difficulty: 3 - C(scripts/seed-catalogue.mjs): assign parent pointers instead of children arrays

- [ ] 2.2 — Run `node scripts/seed-catalogue.mjs` (after clearing existing catalogueItems if necessary) to physically write the new relational data to the Content Lake.
  - Difficulty: 2 - D(database): execute parent-pointer data seed

### Verification — Layer 2

- [ ] V2.1 — Evaluate GROQ `*[_type == "catalogueItem" && defined(parent)]`. Output must yield all non-root nodes (should be 28 nodes, based on 3 roots out of 31 total).
  - Difficulty: 1

- [ ] V2.2 — Evaluate GROQ `*[_type == "catalogueItem" && !defined(parent)]`. Output must yield exactly 3 root nodes.
  - Difficulty: 1

