## Layer 3: Studio UI (The Missing Link)

### Scope Contract
Write a custom Structure Builder (Desk Tool) configuration that instructs Sanity to query the flat documents, read their parent references, and draw a visual, clickable tree hierarchy for the editors.

### DoD

- [ ] 3.1 — In `sanity.config.ts`, register an initial-value template for `catalogueItem` that accepts a `parentId` parameter and dynamically sets the `parent` reference. This guarantees editors can click "Add new" inside a nested sub-level and the node is automatically linked to the correct parent.
  - Difficulty: 3 - A(sanity.config.ts): register initial value template for nested creation

- [ ] 3.2 — In `sanity/structure.ts`: Implement a recursive Structure node algorithm.
  Logic Outline:
  1. Define a function `buildCatalogueTree(S, parentId = null)`
  2. The function generates an `S.documentTypeList("catalogueItem")`.
  3. If `!parentId`, the filter is `!defined(parent)`. If `parentId`, the filter is `parent._ref == $parentId`.
  4. Define the `.child((documentId) => ...)` resolver for the list to return a multi-pane `S.list()` containing:
     - "Edit Details": `S.document().documentId(documentId).schemaType("catalogueItem")`
     - "View Sub-Items": a recursive call to `buildCatalogueTree(S, documentId)`
  - Difficulty: 8 - A(sanity/structure.ts): implement recursive visual tree hierarchy

- [ ] 3.3 — In `sanity/structure.ts`: Replace the standard `S.documentTypeListItem("catalogueItem")` implementation with the root-level call to the new `buildCatalogueTree(S)` function.
  - Difficulty: 1 - C(sanity/structure.ts): wire up custom VFS tree to main structure

### Verification — Layer 3

- [ ] V3.1 — Open Sanity Studio. Click "Catalogue". Confirm you only see the 3 root items.
  - Difficulty: 1
- [ ] V3.2 — Click a root item. Confirm you can navigate into "View Sub-Items" to see its children natively within the Desk Tool pane. Click "Edit Details" to confirm you can edit the folder name/metadata.
  - Difficulty: 1

