## Layer 4: Pre-Compute Script Adaptation

### Scope Contract
Update `scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs` to reconstruct the VFS navigation manifest using the new database standard. Read the `parent` pointers to stitch the tree back together in-memory. The output JSON (`catalogue-index.json`) must remain structurally identical to guarantee zero frontend breakage.

### DoD

- [ ] 4.1 — In `scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs`: Update the GROQ query to fetch the parent reference `parent._ref as parentId` instead of `children`.
  - Difficulty: 1 - C(scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs): update GROQ query for parent refs

- [ ] 4.2 — In `scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs`: Update the in-memory tree reconstruction algorithm. Iterate `allItems`, and if an item has a `parentId`, append it to `itemById[doc.parentId].children`. Filter out any node with a `parentId` to isolate your exact root nodes. The remainder of the `traverse` mapping logic stays 100% untouched.
  - Difficulty: 5 - C(scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs): rebuild tree using adjacency list inversion

- [ ] 4.3 — Run `node scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs`.
  - Difficulty: 1 - D(scripts): rebuild production manifest

### Verification — Layer 4

- [ ] V4.1 — Diff the generated `data/catalogue-index.json` linearly against `catalogue-index.pre-flatten.json`. The newly built manifest must match the old structure flawlessly (identical slug maps, identical tree topology).
  - Difficulty: 2

